---
title: Protect a PDF with a password
description: Encrypt PDF files with a password — free, private, in-browser.
relatedTool: protect-pdf
---

Lock sensitive PDFs with **password encryption** before sharing.

## Steps

1. Open **Protect PDF**.
2. Upload the document.
3. Set a user password (required to open the file).
4. Optionally set an owner password and restrict printing or copying.
5. Download the encrypted PDF.

## Tips

> **Remember your password:** We cannot recover lost passwords — encryption happens locally and we never see your secrets.

- Use **Unlock PDF** if you need to remove a password you know.
- Combine with [Secure PDF workflow](/guides/secure-pdf-workflow) for merge → compress → protect.

